<title>GERMANY: Germany's Hornbach maintains dividend. [CORRECTED]</title>
<headline>Germany's Hornbach maintains dividend. [CORRECTED]</headline>
<dateline>BORNHEIM, Germany 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German building supplies holding group Hornbach Holding AG said on Thursday it would maintain  a dividend of 2.20 marks per five-mark preference share for the year 1995/96.</p>
<p>(Corrects to make clear company will maintain the dividend rather than propose a higher one).</p>
<p>Hornbach also said earnings from ordinary activities in the six months to August 31 slipped to 79 million marks from 84 million in the previous period on turnover up to 986 million marks from 900 million.</p>
<p>The group said it was confident of satisfactory progress in turnover and earnings for the second half of the year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
